# Materialized ONCE from 1Password by chezmoi — the vault is the origin,
# this file is a cache. `create_` semantics: chezmoi writes it only when
# it's MISSING and never evaluates the template otherwise, so `op` (and
# the internet) are a bootstrap dependency, not a tick dependency.
#
# The value is a Tailscale AUTH KEY (admin console → Settings → Keys →
# Auth keys; not reusable, not ephemeral, no tags), and it is
# SINGLE-ENROLMENT in practice: the sidecar reads this file only when its
# state dir says it isn't logged in (TS_AUTH_ONCE), spends the key, and
# never looks again. So unlike gluetun.env the vault copy goes STALE
# after first use — auth keys expire within 90 days regardless — which
# bites only when ~/Docker/forgejo/tailscale is wiped. Re-enrolment:
# mint a fresh key, update the item, delete this file, `chezmoi apply`,
# `docker restart forgejo-tailscale`. See forgejo/README.md
# "Tailnet identity".
TS_AUTHKEY={{ onepasswordRead "op://Wolfe.Lab/forgejo-tailscale/credential" }}
